# F-03 planner-owned acceptance baseline — REVISION 2 (read-only)
#
# Prepared 2026-10-05 by the planner/test-owner session for finding M1 in
# docs/reviews/F-03.md: the returned master contracts did not enforce their kind,
# and the unit acceptance contradicted the frozen spec by accepting a department
# with a severity. No production change is authorised by this revision.
#
# REVISION HISTORY
#   rev 1   (2026-10-05) the first F-03 checkpoint. ARCHIVED byte-for-byte at
#                   docs/handoffs/F-03-tests-rev1.sha256; the archive's own SHA-256
#                   is 2c808615aba136d01cce28cca430ca742c97eba9df03c46aea770de7e3a33a54,
#                   exactly the value pinned in docs/reviews/F-03.md. Do not
#                   regenerate the archive. Running sha256sum -c on it now yields
#                   7 OK / 2 FAILED: the two failures are the artifacts this
#                   revision corrects.
#   rev 2   (2026-10-05) 9 entries, same paths, 2 refreshes. Changes only:
#                   - The contradictory "department with severity is valid"
#                     assertion is replaced by strict kind-specific rejection cases:
#                     wrong-kind fields on simple, violation and gate records, a
#                     missing kind-defining field, and a list whose record kind
#                     disagrees with the list kind.
#                   - Positive coverage for all six legitimate variants, records
#                     and homogeneous lists, is added.
#                   - The feature spec now states the strict, symmetric kind rules
#                     and list homogeneity explicitly.
#                   The real-DB integration suite and the create/update request
#                   validation are unchanged and must stay green.
#
# Other baselines remain unchanged and must continue to verify:
#   docs/handoffs/S-01-tests.sha256            11 entries
#   docs/handoffs/F-01-tests.sha256            14 entries
#   docs/handoffs/F-01-corrections-tests.sha256 10 entries
#   docs/handoffs/F-02-tests.sha256            separate F-02 baseline (rev 5)
#
# Do not regenerate this manifest to fix a failure. Any further revision is a
# numbered rev with its own recorded reason.
